            ('95', 'Role of the National Assembly', 'The National Assembly represents the people, deliberates on and resolves issues of concern to the people, enacts legislation, determines the allocation of national revenue, appropriates funds for expenditure, exercises oversight over national revenue and expenditure, and reviews the conduct in office of the President and other State officers.'),
            ('96', 'Role of the Senate', 'The Senate represents the counties and protects the interests of counties and their governments. The Senate participates in the law-making function of Parliament by considering, debating and approving Bills concerning counties. The Senate determines the allocation of national revenue among counties and exercises oversight over national revenue allocated to county governments.'),
            ('97', 'Membership of the National Assembly', 'The National Assembly consists of 290 members elected for each constituency, 47 women each elected by voters of the counties, 12 members nominated by parliamentary political parties to represent special interests including youth, persons with disabilities and workers, and the Speaker who is an ex officio member.'),
            ('98', 'Membership of the Senate', 'The Senate consists of 47 members each elected by voters of the counties, 16 women members nominated by political parties, 2 members representing youth (one male, one female), 2 members representing persons with disabilities, and the Speaker who is an ex officio member.'),
            ('99', 'Qualifications and disqualifications for election as member of Parliament', 'A person is qualified for election if they are a citizen, are registered as a voter, satisfy any educational requirements, and are nominated by a political party or are an independent candidate.'),
