            ('143', 'Protection from legal proceedings', 'Criminal proceedings shall not be instituted against a person holding the office of President during their tenure. Civil proceedings may be instituted, but shall be held in abeyance during the President\'s tenure.'),
            ('144', 'Removal of President on grounds of incapacity', 'The Deputy President or a member of the National Assembly supported by at least a quarter of members may move a resolution for investigation of the President\'s physical or mental capacity.'),
            ('145', 'Removal of President by impeachment', 'A member of the National Assembly may propose a motion for the impeachment of the President on grounds of gross violation of the Constitution, a crime under national or international law, or gross misconduct.'),
            ('146', 'Vacancy in the office of President', 'The office of President shall become vacant if the President dies, resigns, is removed under Article 144 or 145, or ceases to hold office under Article 142.'),
